        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "context",
            "start": 13,
            "end": 1136,
            "text": "I’m exploring how workflow automation can help businesses manage multi-service platforms similar to Gojek, where customers can book services such as rides, food delivery, grocery shopping, and home services through one platform. As these businesses grow, managing orders, service providers, customer notifications, and payments across different services can become complicated. Here are a few workflows I’m interested in exploring with n8n: Order notifications: Send automatic updates to customers when an order is placed, accepted, or completed. Service provider assignment: Route new requests to suitable providers based on service type and availability. Customer support: Use AI to categorize common customer questions and direct complex issues to a human support agent. Lead and order tracking: Store incoming requests in Google Sheets or a CRM and notify the operations team about pending orders. Daily reports: Generate summaries of completed orders, cancellations, and pending requests. I’d appreciate suggestions, recommended workflow patterns, or examples from anyone who has worked on similar automation projects.",
            "sha256": "016319d62efa2a593f0a5f2d59060139708da87b288c969c803df7025021b34d"
          },
          {
            "kind": "context",
